{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012o1qFrWtxXmaoXpLmhbnYG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Trust\n2\t\n3\t`src/config/trust.ts`, `src/config/canonical.ts`, `src/trust/trust.ts`,\n4\t`src/cli/trust.ts`. Design: ADR-0001, ADR-0003. How CLI tests approve a\n5\tconfig is in `typescript.md`.\n6\t\n7\t- `trustProjection(cfg)` is the security-relevant projection; its\n8\t  `trustHash` covers only endpoint, protocol, credential variable, and\n9\t  prompt-override paths. A new security-relevant config field goes into\n10\t  the projection, or it can change without re-approval.\n11\t- Approvals live in `<git-common-dir>/roast/trust.json`. `roast review`\n12\t  calls `requireTrust` before building scope; untrusted is a usage error\n13\t  (exit 2), never the findings exit.\n14\t- `src/config/trust.ts` (projection, `requiresApproval`, hash v2) is\n15\t  pure. `src/config/canonical.ts` is the only JSON canonicalizer; its\n16\t  input types must be `type` aliases, not interfaces, to be assignable\n17\t  to `CanonicalValue`.\n18\t- `src/trust/trust.ts` takes a trailing `{signal, env}` for git.\n19\t  `src/cli/trust.ts` has the command, `writeTrustSummary` (every value\n20\t  through `textsafe.line`) and `requireTrust(dir, cfg, io)`.\n21\t  `promptNoDefault` (`[y/N]`) lives in `src/cli/terminal.ts`.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fff85d-1c72-432c-ba87-5f843ff95960","uuid":"a47490b9-e292-49aa-9c08-da84af2ac529","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:46:21.533Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-04-init-trust-offer/docs/agents/trust.md","content":"# Trust\n\n`src/config/trust.ts`, `src/config/canonical.ts`, `src/trust/trust.ts`,\n`src/cli/trust.ts`. Design: ADR-0001, ADR-0003. How CLI tests approve a\nconfig is in `typescript.md`.\n\n- `trustProjection(cfg)` is the security-relevant projection; its\n  `trustHash` covers only endpoint, protocol, credential variable, and\n  prompt-override paths. A new security-relevant config field goes into\n  the projection, or it can change without re-approval.\n- Approvals live in `<git-common-dir>/roast/trust.json`. `roast review`\n  calls `requireTrust` before building scope; untrusted is a usage error\n  (exit 2), never the findings exit.\n- `src/config/trust.ts` (projection, `requiresApproval`, hash v2) is\n  pure. `src/config/canonical.ts` is the only JSON canonicalizer; its\n  input types must be `type` aliases, not interfaces, to be assignable\n  to `CanonicalValue`.\n- `src/trust/trust.ts` takes a trailing `{signal, env}` for git.\n  `src/cli/trust.ts` has the command, `writeTrustSummary` (every value\n  through `textsafe.line`) and `requireTrust(dir, cfg, io)`.\n  `promptNoDefault` (`[y/N]`) lives in `src/cli/terminal.ts`.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012o1qFrWtxXmaoXpLmhbnYG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
