{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y1PicJCsPLUvyVchEd7N4N","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 04: Trust offer after `init` writes a config that needs approval\n2\t\n3\t**What to build:** When the project config `init` just wrote needs trust\n4\tapproval (`requiresApproval` on its `trustProjection`, as happens with a\n5\tcustom endpoint or key variable from ticket 03) and the terminals are\n6\tinteractive, `init` prints the same summary `npx roast trust` prints\n7\t(`writeTrustSummary`) and asks for approval with a No default\n8\t(`promptNoDefault`). Yes records the approval with the existing trust\n9\thash, exactly as `npx roast trust` would, so the first review is not\n10\trefused. No records nothing and prints a hint to run `npx roast trust`\n11\tlater; `init` still succeeds. The offer comes after the login offer and\n12\tthe custom key-variable hints. Without interactive terminals there is no\n13\toffer. ADR-0001 and ADR-0003 hold: approval is explicit, shows every\n14\tsecurity-relevant value, and uses the existing hash.\n15\t\n16\tDocs: README \"### 2. Create the project config\" (the trust offer).\n17\t\n18\t**Blocked by:** 03\n19\t\n20\t**Touches:** `src/cli/init.ts`, `src/cli/trust.ts` (`writeTrustSummary`),\n21\t`src/config/trust.ts` (`trustProjection`, `requiresApproval`,\n22\t`trustHash`), `src/trust/trust.ts` (`approve`, `isApproved`),\n23\t`src/cli/terminal.ts` (`promptNoDefault`), `test/cli/init.ts`,\n24\t`README.md`\n25\t\n26\t**Status:** ready-for-agent\n27\t\n28\t- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered Yes leaves the\n29\t      written config approved for this clone\n30\t- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered No (or Enter)\n31\t      leaves the config not approved, and `init` exits successfully\n32\t- [ ] A config using only built-in providers gets no trust offer and\n33\t      reads no stdin for one\n34\t- [ ] EOF at the trust offer leaves the config not approved and the\n35\t      project config written\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fff85d-1c72-432c-ba87-5f843ff95960","uuid":"2a98ac12-0f91-461f-b1cd-c97d1d56173d","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:46:29.856Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-04-init-trust-offer/.scratch/init-model-prompts/issues/04-init-trust-offer.md","content":"# 04: Trust offer after `init` writes a config that needs approval\n\n**What to build:** When the project config `init` just wrote needs trust\napproval (`requiresApproval` on its `trustProjection`, as happens with a\ncustom endpoint or key variable from ticket 03) and the terminals are\ninteractive, `init` prints the same summary `npx roast trust` prints\n(`writeTrustSummary`) and asks for approval with a No default\n(`promptNoDefault`). Yes records the approval with the existing trust\nhash, exactly as `npx roast trust` would, so the first review is not\nrefused. No records nothing and prints a hint to run `npx roast trust`\nlater; `init` still succeeds. The offer comes after the login offer and\nthe custom key-variable hints. Without interactive terminals there is no\noffer. ADR-0001 and ADR-0003 hold: approval is explicit, shows every\nsecurity-relevant value, and uses the existing hash.\n\nDocs: README \"### 2. Create the project config\" (the trust offer).\n\n**Blocked by:** 03\n\n**Touches:** `src/cli/init.ts`, `src/cli/trust.ts` (`writeTrustSummary`),\n`src/config/trust.ts` (`trustProjection`, `requiresApproval`,\n`trustHash`), `src/trust/trust.ts` (`approve`, `isApproved`),\n`src/cli/terminal.ts` (`promptNoDefault`), `test/cli/init.ts`,\n`README.md`\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered Yes leaves the\n      written config approved for this clone\n- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered No (or Enter)\n      leaves the config not approved, and `init` exits successfully\n- [ ] A config using only built-in providers gets no trust offer and\n      reads no stdin for one\n- [ ] EOF at the trust offer leaves the config not approved and the\n      project config written\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y1PicJCsPLUvyVchEd7N4N","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
