{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NgC54H7Jbw2n4XVB7xXR7m","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-04-init-trust-offer/.scratch/init-model-prompts/issues/04-init-trust-offer.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fff85d-1c72-432c-ba87-5f843ff95960","uuid":"16514d1d-e623-440b-8d25-9b8c5528a188","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:23:11.005Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-04-init-trust-offer/.scratch/init-model-prompts/issues/04-init-trust-offer.md","oldString":"- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered Yes leaves the\n      written config approved for this clone\n- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered No (or Enter)\n      leaves the config not approved, and `init` exits successfully\n- [ ] A config using only built-in providers gets no trust offer and\n      reads no stdin for one\n- [ ] EOF at the trust offer leaves the config not approved and the\n      project config written","newString":"- [x] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered Yes leaves the\n      written config approved for this clone\n- [x] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered No (or Enter)\n      leaves the config not approved, and `init` exits successfully\n- [x] A config using only built-in providers gets no trust offer and\n      reads no stdin for one\n- [x] EOF at the trust offer leaves the config not approved and the\n      project config written","originalFile":"# 04: Trust offer after `init` writes a config that needs approval\n\n**What to build:** When the project config `init` just wrote needs trust\napproval (`requiresApproval` on its `trustProjection`, as happens with a\ncustom endpoint or key variable from ticket 03) and the terminals are\ninteractive, `init` prints the same summary `npx roast trust` prints\n(`writeTrustSummary`) and asks for approval with a No default\n(`promptNoDefault`). Yes records the approval with the existing trust\nhash, exactly as `npx roast trust` would, so the first review is not\nrefused. No records nothing and prints a hint to run `npx roast trust`\nlater; `init` still succeeds. The offer comes after the login offer and\nthe custom key-variable hints. Without interactive terminals there is no\noffer. ADR-0001 and ADR-0003 hold: approval is explicit, shows every\nsecurity-relevant value, and uses the existing hash.\n\nDocs: README \"### 2. Create the project config\" (the trust offer).\n\n**Blocked by:** 03\n\n**Touches:** `src/cli/init.ts`, `src/cli/trust.ts` (`writeTrustSummary`),\n`src/config/trust.ts` (`trustProjection`, `requiresApproval`,\n`trustHash`), `src/trust/trust.ts` (`approve`, `isApproved`),\n`src/cli/terminal.ts` (`promptNoDefault`), `test/cli/init.ts`,\n`README.md`\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered Yes leaves the\n      written config approved for this clone\n- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered No (or Enter)\n      leaves the config not approved, and `init` exits successfully\n- [ ] A config using only built-in providers gets no trust offer and\n      reads no stdin for one\n- [ ] EOF at the trust offer leaves the config not approved and the\n      project config written\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":11,"newStart":25,"newLines":11,"lines":[" "," **Status:** ready-for-agent"," ","-- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered Yes leaves the","+- [x] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered Yes leaves the","       written config approved for this clone","-- [ ] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered No (or Enter)","+- [x] A custom endpoint with the trust offer answered No (or Enter)","       leaves the config not approved, and `init` exits successfully","-- [ ] A config using only built-in providers gets no trust offer and","+- [x] A config using only built-in providers gets no trust offer and","       reads no stdin for one","-- [ ] EOF at the trust offer leaves the config not approved and the","+- [x] EOF at the trust offer leaves the config not approved and the","       project config written"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NgC54H7Jbw2n4XVB7xXR7m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
