{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YLuFTyPhJJTsygkG2xausP","type":"tool_result","content":"68\t### 2. Create the project config\n69\t\n70\t```sh\n71\tnpx roast init\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\tThis writes `.roast.json` in the current directory and adds `/.roast/` to\n75\t`.gitignore`. Command `init` picks each role's provider from its\n76\tmodel ID:\n77\t\n78\t- a bare Claude model ID (`claude-opus-5-5`) uses Anthropic's Messages API\n79\t- a bare OpenAI model ID (including Codex, `gpt-6.1-terra`) uses OpenAI's\n80\t  Responses API\n81\t- a slash-form ID, `<vendor>/<model>` with an optional `:<variant>`\n82\t  (`anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`, `meta-llama/llama-4:free`), uses\n83\t  [OpenRouter](#openrouter).\n84\t\n85\tEither model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models\n86\tfrom different providers for each role.\n87\t\n88\tIn an interactive terminal, `init` prompts for each role's provider\n89\tand model when the corresponding flag is missing. The provider menu\n90\tlists Anthropic, OpenAI, and OpenRouter; each model prompt suggests a\n91\tdefault that Enter accepts. For a model that no built-in provider\n92\tserves, edit `.roast.json` by hand\n93\t(see [Project config](#project-config)).\n94\t\n95\tWithout an interactive terminal, `init` writes placeholder model IDs\n96\tand prints a hint naming `--finder-model` and `--verifier-model`. A\n97\treview refuses to run until you replace the placeholders in\n98\t`.roast.json`.\n99\t\n100\tIn the terminal, `init` then offers to log in to each provider\n101\tthat has no credential yet (see [Login and logout](#login-and-logout)).\n102\t\n103\tFlag `--no-login` skips the login process.\n104\t\n105\t\n106\t#### `init` Example\n107\t\n108\tClaude as the finder and Codex as the verifier:\n109\t\n110\t```sh\n111\tnpx roast init --finder-model 'claude-opus-5-5' \\\n112\t  --verifier-model 'gpt-6.1-terra'\n113\t```\n114\t\n115\t`init` refuses to overwrite an existing `.roast.json`.\n116\t\n117\t\n118\t### 3. Login\n119\t\n120\tIf you skipped the login process during `init`, log in now:\n121\t\n122\t```sh\n123\tnpx roast login\n124\t```\n125\t\n126\tWith no argument, `login` reads `.roast.json` and logs in to each built-in\n127\tprovider that has no credentials yet. For Anthropic and OpenAI,\n128\tit opens the provider's API-keys page. Create a key and paste it into the\n129\thidden prompt. For OpenRouter, it opens OpenRouter in your browser and\n130\treceives a new key when you approve. The key is stored for this project\n131\tinside `.git`, so it is never committed, and every later review, including\n132\tthe [pre-commit gate](#pre-commit-gate), finds it.\n133\t\n134\tEnvironment variables still work and take precedence over a stored key,\n135\twhich suits CI:\n136\t\n137\t```sh\n138\texport OPENAI_API_KEY='...'      # platform.openai.com/api-keys\n139\texport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY='...'   # console.anthropic.com/settings/keys\n140\texport OPENROUTER_API_KEY='...'  # openrouter.ai/settings/keys\n141\t```\n142\t\n143\tTo see which models an OpenAI key can use:\n144\t\n145\t```sh\n146\tcurl -s https://api.openai.com/v1/models \\\n147\t  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_API_KEY\" | jq -r '.data[].id'"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fff85d-1c72-432c-ba87-5f843ff95960","uuid":"13be9474-805a-4488-b97c-ceaffcf75502","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:23:17.144Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.init-model-prompts-04-init-trust-offer/README.md","content":"### 2. Create the project config\n\n```sh\nnpx roast init\n```\n\nThis writes `.roast.json` in the current directory and adds `/.roast/` to\n`.gitignore`. Command `init` picks each role's provider from its\nmodel ID:\n\n- a bare Claude model ID (`claude-opus-5-5`) uses Anthropic's Messages API\n- a bare OpenAI model ID (including Codex, `gpt-6.1-terra`) uses OpenAI's\n  Responses API\n- a slash-form ID, `<vendor>/<model>` with an optional `:<variant>`\n  (`anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`, `meta-llama/llama-4:free`), uses\n  [OpenRouter](#openrouter).\n\nEither model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models\nfrom different providers for each role.\n\nIn an interactive terminal, `init` prompts for each role's provider\nand model when the corresponding flag is missing. The provider menu\nlists Anthropic, OpenAI, and OpenRouter; each model prompt suggests a\ndefault that Enter accepts. For a model that no built-in provider\nserves, edit `.roast.json` by hand\n(see [Project config](#project-config)).\n\nWithout an interactive terminal, `init` writes placeholder model IDs\nand prints a hint naming `--finder-model` and `--verifier-model`. A\nreview refuses to run until you replace the placeholders in\n`.roast.json`.\n\nIn the terminal, `init` then offers to log in to each provider\nthat has no credential yet (see [Login and logout](#login-and-logout)).\n\nFlag `--no-login` skips the login process.\n\n\n#### `init` Example\n\nClaude as the finder and Codex as the verifier:\n\n```sh\nnpx roast init --finder-model 'claude-opus-5-5' \\\n  --verifier-model 'gpt-6.1-terra'\n```\n\n`init` refuses to overwrite an existing `.roast.json`.\n\n\n### 3. Login\n\nIf you skipped the login process during `init`, log in now:\n\n```sh\nnpx roast login\n```\n\nWith no argument, `login` reads `.roast.json` and logs in to each built-in\nprovider that has no credentials yet. For Anthropic and OpenAI,\nit opens the provider's API-keys page. Create a key and paste it into the\nhidden prompt. For OpenRouter, it opens OpenRouter in your browser and\nreceives a new key when you approve. The key is stored for this project\ninside `.git`, so it is never committed, and every later review, including\nthe [pre-commit gate](#pre-commit-gate), finds it.\n\nEnvironment variables still work and take precedence over a stored key,\nwhich suits CI:\n\n```sh\nexport OPENAI_API_KEY='...'      # platform.openai.com/api-keys\nexport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY='...'   # console.anthropic.com/settings/keys\nexport OPENROUTER_API_KEY='...'  # openrouter.ai/settings/keys\n```\n\nTo see which models an OpenAI key can use:\n\n```sh\ncurl -s https://api.openai.com/v1/models \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_API_KEY\" | jq -r '.data[].id'","numLines":80,"startLine":68,"totalLines":656}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YLuFTyPhJJTsygkG2xausP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
